 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "As if a glass element inside the lens had come loose and rattles on its mount. Every real jolt and swing of the camera knocks it off centre for a moment: one side of the picture goes soft, colours fringe apart toward that side and the corner darkens, then the element springs back, overshoots a little and the picture clicks sharp again. A still shot stays exactly as it was.",
